# Forbidden remote: objectcomputing/quickfast

**Never** commit, push, force-push, create branches on, or open pull requests against [objectcomputing/quickfast](https://github.com/objectcomputing/quickfast) (OCI upstream).

## Hard bans

- Do **not** set `origin` (or any push remote) to `https://github.com/objectcomputing/quickfast` or `git@github.com:objectcomputing/quickfast.git`
- Do **not** `git push` / `git push -u` to any remote whose URL contains `objectcomputing/quickfast`
- Do **not** `gh pr create` targeting `objectcomputing/quickfast` (base or head repo)
- Do **not** suggest opening a PR, syncing writable remotes, or “contributing upstream” to that repo unless the user explicitly overrides in the current message

## Allowed remotes

Work only against this fork (or other remotes the user names):

- [vs-76/quickfast-ng](https://github.com/vs-76/quickfast-ng) — default `origin`

Upstream may be added **read-only** for fetch/rebase if needed:

```bash
# ✅ fetch-only mirror (no push)
git remote add upstream https://github.com/objectcomputing/quickfast.git
git remote set-url --push upstream DISABLE
```

```bash
# ❌ never
git push origin ...   # if origin is objectcomputing/quickfast
git push upstream ...
gh pr create --repo objectcomputing/quickfast ...
```

If a command would touch that repo for write, **stop**, warn the user, and use `vs-76/quickfast-ng` instead.
